                                            "In a delicious manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0645878a-d7f4-40fe-bddb-52ac7862d323",
                        "source_entry_id": "0099733a-0f94-3bc1-b706-5fc5d7f2a782",
                        "target_lang_word": "delightfully",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "delightfully",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d0e0346-b2fc-3a3d-acb4-385a16641d1b",
                                        "entry_id": "2bf39cc5-05aa-3e7f-ac87-129f9452e65c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a delightful manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86e71b32-6783-45bd-9e87-5e2230602692",
                                                "sense_id": "8d0e0346-b2fc-3a3d-acb4-385a16641d1b",
                                                "text": "The result, disappointingly, is a scattershot work that is, by turns, entertaining and wearisome, energetic and hokey, delightfully evocative and cheaply sensational; dead-on in its conjuring of zeitgeist-y atmospherics, but often slow-footed and ham-handed in its orchestration of social details."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2354e60d-97b9-4a01-aacc-6059b39a65b8",
                        "source_entry_id": "0099733a-0f94-3bc1-b706-5fc5d7f2a782",
                        "target_lang_word": "exquisitely",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "exquisitely",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab0bcc09-c620-3293-94be-0e6dbb0774ab",
                                        "entry_id": "097c46ab-f217-3c2d-812b-1093c94bf571",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an exquisite manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "59adec98-be1b-4aae-8e9a-1d2afdb91052",
                                                "sense_id": "ab0bcc09-c620-3293-94be-0e6dbb0774ab",
                                                "text": "Over the fish-dish — something sole-like, exquisitely seethed in a strange sauce, garnished with roots and fruits of the country — Tommy became sentimental."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a96cd4f-d925-32d8-a4a1-90fe9c06d64c",
                                        "entry_id": "097c46ab-f217-3c2d-812b-1093c94bf571",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Exceedingly; in the highest degree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67857444-977b-439a-8503-c0b135b7a046",
                                                "sense_id": "6a96cd4f-d925-32d8-a4a1-90fe9c06d64c",
                                                "text": "There was something exquisitely painful in the memories that crowded upon his mind: a thousand of Constance's daily acts of affection rose before him: neyer till this moment had he felt them unrequited; but now they were remembered like a reproach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "208af548-4a34-46ad-b7a3-bae4bb70fb5a",
                                                "sense_id": "6a96cd4f-d925-32d8-a4a1-90fe9c06d64c",
                                                "text": "They danced on silently, softly. Their feet played tricks to the beat of the tireless measure, that exquisitely asinine blare which is England's punishment for having lost America."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c6f638d4-0b0c-419c-ba8b-a6e9035f93ca",
                        "source_entry_id": "0099733a-0f94-3bc1-b706-5fc5d7f2a782",
